---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import NextPageLink from "../../components/NextPageLink.astro";
import { withBase } from "../../lib/paths";

const learned = [
  "A thin margin with more money poured into it is still a thin margin, now with one more person waiting to be paid.",
  "The farmer's problem is buying at retail and selling at wholesale, not a shortage of investors.",
  "Collecting other people's money for farm seasons is a regulated business, not a side project.",
  "Banks, buyers, and dairies already lend against a season. The useful work is making a small group worth lending to.",
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Season Trust · Sundharesan Kumaresan"
  description="Season Trust was a first bet on outside money funding farm seasons. It is parked while iyal works on farm margins first."
>
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto max-w-page px-6 pt-16 pb-16">
    <a href={withBase("/to")} class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-kicker text-text-muted transition-colors hover:text-text">&larr; To</a>

    <header class="mt-8">
      <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-kicker text-accent">A parked bet</p>
      <h1 data-reveal class="reveal-tracking mt-3 max-w-[12ch] font-serif text-display-page font-semibold leading-[0.98]">Season Trust</h1>
      <p data-reveal class="reveal-scale mt-8 max-w-[25ch] font-serif text-statement font-semibold leading-[1.08]">Outside money into farm seasons. Parked, on purpose.</p>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-[68ch] space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text">
        <p>Season Trust was my first bet: let people from outside the village fund a farming season, and let repayment follow the harvest instead of a calendar.</p>
        <p>I've parked it. Money poured into a thin margin just adds someone else who wants a share of it. The margin has to work first. When it does, banks and buyers are better places for that money to come from than me.</p>
        <p>The work continues in <a href={withBase("/iyal")} class="font-script text-3xl leading-none text-accent transition-colors hover:text-accent-hover">iyal</a>, which now asks a plainer question: what does a season cost, what does it earn, and who keeps the difference?</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="mt-20 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-[0.75fr_1.25fr] md:border-t md:border-border md:pt-12">
      <div>
        <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-kicker text-accent">What changed my mind</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="max-w-[68ch] border-t border-border">
        {learned.map((item) => (
          <li class="border-b border-border py-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text">{item}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20 border-t-2 border-stellar pt-10">
      <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-kicker text-accent">Current status</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 max-w-[22ch] font-serif text-entry font-semibold leading-[1.05]">Parked. Not abandoned, not open for funding.</h2>
      <div class="mt-8 max-w-[68ch] space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text">
        <p>I'm not taking money for this. If you've seen outside money help a farming season, or watched it go badly, I'd like to hear how it actually worked.</p>
        <a href={withBase("/contact")} class="group inline-block font-serif text-statement font-semibold leading-none text-text transition-colors hover:text-accent">Share your perspective <span class="adv-arrow text-accent">&rarr;</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <NextPageLink href="/to/sports-development">The Long Game</NextPageLink>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
